# implements-port slice 11 (B2; Q43, the author: a cell of `rows:` is an argument -- an atom, a Structure, an array
# -- through the common gate, no exceptions; refusing a cell that is not one atom is a bug): unit_s7_prim_cross
# over its own convert.lm2 whose first row has a Structure cell (tests/unit_s7_conv_cellstruct_table.lm2).  The
# Structure is one cell, the rows stay aligned, size_t -> int still finds its receiver: Entry 7.  Before, the
# Structure was walked into and dropped, and the rows were refused as not whole.
fn: go () int
    int: a 1
    size_t: b 2U
    a: b
    return: a

int: k
k: go()
if: k = 2
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 1; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
